    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g89s00p",
      "content": "<img></img>Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP) are guidelines to the government for creating a just and welfare-oriented society. They are contained in Part IV of the Constitution of India (Articles 36–51). Although they are not enforceable by courts, they are fundamental in the governance of the country."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Constitutional Part",
          "value": "Part IV",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Article Range",
          "value": "Articles 36–51",
          "icon": "calendar"
        },
        {
          "label": "Categories",
          "value": "3 Principles",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "Legal Nature",
          "value": "Non-Justiciable",
          "icon": "check"
        }
      ],
      "id": "1z5llur"
    },
    {
      "id": "wsd9j8o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning and Importance of DPSP"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP) are contained in Part IV of the Indian Constitution.",
        "DPSPs are broadly classified into Socialist, Gandhian, and Liberal–Intellectual principles.",
        "Unlike Fundamental Rights, Directive Principles are non-justiciable in nature.",
        "DPSPs aim to establish social and economic democracy in the country."
      ],
      "id": "9a4o3ee"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tiku9e2",
      "content": "• DPSP aim to establish social and economic democracy in India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i89cf1w",
      "content": "• They guide the government in making laws and policies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6fe2q90",
      "content": "• They promote welfare of the people."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mk8rot7",
      "content": "• They help in establishing a welfare state."
    },
    {
