      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Difference between Fundamental Rights and DPSP"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "DPSPs were borrowed from the Irish Constitution of 1937.",
        "Fundamental Rights aim at political democracy, whereas DPSPs aim at socio-economic democracy.",
        "Article 37 explicitly states that DPSPs are fundamental in the governance of the country, though non-enforceable by courts."
      ],
      "id": "hfjnnsy"
    },
